  <data name="MeetingAttendee_Requirements_Title" xml:space="preserve"><value>Requirements</value></data>
  <data name="MeetingAttendee_Requirements_Teams" xml:space="preserve"><value>•  A Microsoft Teams meeting link.</value></data>
  <data name="MeetingAttendee_Requirements_Lobby" xml:space="preserve"><value>•  A meeting host must admit the assistant from the lobby before it can transcribe.</value></data>
  <data name="MeetingAttendee_Requirements_FirstRun" xml:space="preserve"><value>•  On first use the automation browser is downloaded once (needs internet that time); later meetings reuse it.</value></data>
  <data name="MeetingAttendee_Requirements_Model" xml:space="preserve"><value>•  Audio is transcribed locally — a speech-to-text model must be available; optional speaker recognition downloads an extra model when enabled in Settings.</value></data>
  <data name="MeetingAttendee_Requirements_Desktop" xml:space="preserve"><value>•  An interactive Windows desktop with a working audio device.</value></data>
  <data name="MeetingAttendee_Requirements_Background" xml:space="preserve"><value>•  While attending, Pia runs a bundled browser and a Node-based automation helper in the background — both ship with Pia, no separate install needed.</value></data>
