  <data name="DirectTrans_Disclaimer_Title" xml:space="preserve"><value>Before you start</value></data>
  <data name="DirectTrans_Disclaimer_Body" xml:space="preserve"><value>This transcribes your microphone and this device's system audio, entirely on this device. Nothing is sent anywhere. Everyone speaking into your microphone appears as "me" in the transcript.</value></data>
  <data name="DirectTrans_Disclaimer_ConsentExplainer" xml:space="preserve"><value>People on the other side (system audio) are not transcribed until they say a consent sentence naming Pia — until then their speech is only checked for that sentence, then discarded.</value></data>
  <data name="DirectTrans_Disclaimer_CrossTalkLimitation" xml:space="preserve"><value>Note: overlapping speech (cross-talk) can occasionally be misattributed to the wrong speaker.</value></data>
  <data name="DirectTrans_Disclaimer_ShortUtteranceLimitation" xml:space="preserve"><value>Very short remarks (under about 1.5 seconds) are dropped and never transcribed, consented or not.</value></data>
  <data name="DirectTrans_Disclaimer_ConsentSentence_Heading" xml:space="preserve"><value>A participant can say, for example:</value></data>
  <data name="DirectTrans_Disclaimer_ConsentSentence_En" xml:space="preserve"><value>My name is [Name] and I accept that Pia is recording this conversation.</value></data>
  <data name="DirectTrans_Disclaimer_ConsentSentence_De" xml:space="preserve"><value>Mein Name ist [Name] und ich bin einverstanden, dass Pia dieses Gespräch aufzeichnet.</value></data>
  <data name="DirectTrans_Disclaimer_ConsentSentence_Fr" xml:space="preserve"><value>Je m’appelle [Nom] et j’accepte que Pia enregistre cette conversation.</value></data>
  <data name="DirectTrans_Disclaimer_Accept" xml:space="preserve"><value>I have informed everyone present and I'm ready to start</value></data>
